# Amendment #53 — self-upgrade seal-bookkeeping retrofit

2026-04-26. Retrofits the seal-bookkeeping infrastructure that
self-upgrade did not receive at original seal time
(2026-04-19 14:12 per `docs/rebuild/STATE.md`). Same shape as
the memory-system retrofit (amendment #8) and the graceful-
degradation + observability-aggregator retrofit (chore commit
`7d462e3`, 2026-04-22).

Surface added (self-upgrade — tests + bookkeeping only):

  - `self-upgrade/tests/test_no_sealed_amendments.py` (new) —
    AC.SU-sb.1. Mirrors the memory-system / graceful-degradation
    pattern. Two tests: `test_B23_seal_commit_pinning_pattern`
    (structural pinning — file contains `BASELINE = ` literal,
    `SEAL_COMMIT_PATH`, and the `{BASELINE}..{seal}` diff form
    routing through `_seal_commit()`) and
    `test_B20_only_self_upgrade_surfaces_changed` (runtime
    `git diff --name-only BASELINE..SEAL_COMMIT` confined to
    the allowed-prefix tuple).
  - `self-upgrade/tests/SEAL_COMMIT` (new) — AC.SU-sb.2.
    Sidecar carrying the authoritative seal SHA. Initial value
    = pre-amendment tip; advanced to the seal commit SHA by
    `pos-amend seal`.
  - `self-upgrade/seals/.gitkeep` (new) — AC.SU-sb.3.
    Placeholder so the seals/ directory tracks in git, ready
    for future `pos-amend seal` runs to write
    `SEAL_COMMIT.<slug>` narrative files into. Mirrors the
    directory pattern at `primary-persona/seals/`,
    `workspace-bootstrap/seals/`, `objective-tracker/seals/`,
    `telegram-interface/seals/`, and
    `hands-off-lifecycle/seals/`.

Zero edits to `self-upgrade/src/` — retrofit-only. Existing
self-upgrade test suite stays green (120 tests pre-amendment;
122 tests post-amendment — the two new pinning + diff-scope
tests).

BASELINE `edf6429` (pre-amendment tip = current HEAD at plan
authoring, post amendment #52 SHA-record commit). The
BASELINE..HEAD diff window opens empty at amendment-commit
time per the standard retrofit pattern; future amendments
advance both BASELINE (via `pos-amend apply`) and SEAL_COMMIT
(via `pos-amend seal`).

With this amendment, all 14 sealed components carry the
seal-diff bookkeeping pipeline (12 had it pre-amendment;
self-upgrade is #13; safety-layer's seal-diff test is a
monkey-patch import guard with a separate shape and is not
counted in this 14). The cross-component seal-diff sweep gains
a new entry for self-upgrade. BB-feat (clause-(h) LLM-merge,
next amendment) re-dispatches against the post-retrofit tip
and is now enforceable through the standard seal-diff window.

Out of scope (retrofit-only):
  - Clause-(h) LLM-merge implementation (BB-feat, next
    amendment).
  - Any source edits to `self-upgrade/src/`.
  - Reviving the prior-BB stale clause-h plan-doc / builder-
    plan / vars (untracked files left for BB-feat dispatch).

With this amendment, the harness's seal-diff substrate is at
parity across every Phase 2 sealed component.
